                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The **GEO Stack** is a five-layer framework for **Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)**\u2014improving how likely AI search systems are to find, understand, trust, remember, and cite a brand\u2019s content.[2][4]\n\nIts layers are:\n\n1. **Retrieval Probability** \u2014 Make content discoverable and indexable by AI crawlers.\n2. **Extractability** \u2014 Structure information so AI systems can parse and accurately quote it.\n3. **Entity Reinforcement** \u2014 Maintain consistent brand, product, author, and organization identities across the web.\n4. **Structural Authority** \u2014 Demonstrate credibility through high-quality citations, backlinks, expertise signals, and trusted references.\n5. **System Memory** \u2014 Keep information fresh and consistently reinforced so AI systems continue to recall and cite it.[4][5]\n\nThe framework is intended to be applied from the bottom up: if content cannot be retrieved or extracted, stronger authority signals are unlikely to help. Unlike traditional SEO, which primarily targets rankings and clicks, the GEO Stack focuses on **AI-generated visibility, representation accuracy, and citation frequency**.[5][6]",
